<title>USA: Circuit Systems says to repurchase shares.</title>
<headline>Circuit Systems says to repurchase shares.</headline>
<dateline>ELK GROVE VILLAGE, Ill. 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Circuit Systems Inc said it plans to repurchase up to an additional 100,000 shares of its common stock.</p>
<p>The purchases will be made at the market price either on the open market or in privately negotiated transactions, said the printed circuit board maker.</p>
<p>&quot;Earlier this year the board authorized the repurchase of up to 250,000 shares, of which 248,000 shares were repurchased. There are approximately 5,100,000 shares outstanding,&quot; Circuit Systems said.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
